[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi everyone! I've been working on a classical field theory and formalized a chain of results that effectively demonstrates an ER=EPR solution that breaks the classical correlation limit.</p>\n<p>However, I have a question about Lean4 architecture. What's the best way to present a conclusion like this? It involves several independent results, such as the correlation statistics, compliance with Bell's theorem, and compliance with the no-signaling theorem. Should I prove these individually, and then have a summary theorem that groups all of the results together?</p>\n<p>Here's a minimal example (the complete code is <a href=\"https://github.com/LoganEvans/chiral-gauge-dynamics/blob/dev/CGD/Quantum/Entanglement/Synthesis.lean#L120\">here</a>):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- ==========================================</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- 1. MINIMIZED MOCK DEFS (No Namespaces)</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- ==========================================</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DerivativeExponential</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">exp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BellsTheorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SpacetimePoint</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SL2C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Sl2cGaugeField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SpacetimePoint</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SL2C</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PhysicalUniverse</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">sd_sector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Sl2cGaugeField</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fluxTubeFrame</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SpacetimePoint</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SL2C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isFluxTube</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Sl2cGaugeField</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SpacetimePoint</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">straightLinePath</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SpacetimePoint</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">curvatureSl2c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Sl2cGaugeField</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SpacetimePoint</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">urbantkeMetric</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">physicalCorrelation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">matrixExp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PhysicalUniverse</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- ==========================================</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- 2. THE ARCHITECTURAL QUESTION</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- ==========================================</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cgdEntanglementSynthesis</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">matrixExp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DerivativeExponential</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matrixExp</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PhysicalUniverse</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SpacetimePoint</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h_tube</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isFluxTube</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pu.sd_sector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pu.sd_sector.val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">straightLinePath</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fluxTubeFrame</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">straightLinePath</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- 1. Violation of the Classical Limit (Bell's Inequality)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EuclideanSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">physicalCorrelation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matrixExp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"n\">physicalCorrelation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matrixExp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">physicalCorrelation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matrixExp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- 2. Compliance with Bell's Theorem (Rejection of LHVs)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">BellsTheorem</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- 3. Compliance with No-Signaling (Topological Metric Degeneracy)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">urbantkeMetric</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">curvatureSl2c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pu.sd_sector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">det</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">end</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is creating a conjoint summary like this the best way to show the result, or is there a more idiomatic approach? Maybe I should keep the individual components separate?</p>",
        "id": 614416557,
        "sender_full_name": "Logan Evans",
        "timestamp": 1785794685
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If the results are independent, you should leave them as separate theorems. If they have many hypotheses in common, you should use <code>variable</code> blocks.</p>",
        "id": 614419266,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1785796456
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>IMO <code>And</code> (<code>∧</code>) is reserved for: bi-implication (where the idea is demonstrate that <code>A ∧ B ↔ C</code>), grouping conclusions that appear under binders (e.g. existential quantification <code>∃ a b c, A ∧ B</code> where one has to assert that <code>A</code> and <code>B</code> hold under the <em>same</em> witness) and conclusions where the conjunct doesn't make sense to be split at all. I think there's few exceptions. On the point of atomicity: will any user of your theorem have to constantly take the nth projection to get which result they want? Was there any natural language reason <code>P ∧ Q</code> was picked over <code>Q ∧ P</code>? If a user wants only <code>P</code>, but to get there, do they have to satisfy not only the preconditions for <code>P</code> but also those of <code>Q</code>, even though they only wanted <code>P</code>?</p>",
        "id": 614420598,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1785797231
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>These results are mathematically independent, so as you suggest, I can keep them as separate theorems. In fact, now that I'm thinking about it, only the correlation statistics mathematically matter. The Bell's theorem and no-signaling theorem results are only really there to address what I expect to be the first responses to the correlation statistics theorem. How was I able to construct entanglement, where the deterministic nature of a classical theorem seems to imply that a theory should be both realist and local? Does the solution break Lorentz invariance by creating time paradoxes? Those concerns absolutely need to be addressed, but as you say, any user of the theorem shouldn't need to care about satisfying the no-go theorems.</p>",
        "id": 614422087,
        "sender_full_name": "Logan Evans",
        "timestamp": 1785798252
    }
]